  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\n\nIt is quite warm across the forecast area at this hour, but it\nis a pretty classic cold advection pattern for weather\novernight. Upslope rain showers (and snow at elevation), plenty\nof stratocumulus, and gusty west northwest winds are expected\ninto early Sat. One minor adjustment was to blend in MOS/raw 2 m\ntemps as the NBM is bias correcting towards radiational cooling\ntoo much after such a prolonged stretch of high pressure. \n\nSat will begin gusty but gradually see those winds diminish\nduring the day. It will be much colder however, with highs a\ngood 10 to 15 degrees below today. But heading into the evening\ntemps will be falling from the 40s into the 30s. \n\nMainly dry conditions are likely to persist thru at least the \nmiddle of next week with fluctuating temps, although on the\nwhole it should average warmer than normal. The next chance for\nany meaningful rainfall looks like it may arrive late in the\nweek, but NWP continues to highlight a very low confidence\nscenario as it keeps pushing rain back and/or shifting the storm\ntrack around.",
